From 22be05e8b97c74ae7135817a50c8d51c8d00eb46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:34:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: clearer test runner output, and JSON lines and summary
 output
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Console (test_framework/reporting.py):
- One line per finished test: ✓/○/✖, name and duration. The skip reason
  is shown for skipped tests, and the status for timeouts and crashes.
- On a terminal, one updating status line (done/total, failures, tests
  still running) replaces the "<test> started" lines and the old
  every-10-seconds "Running jobs" line. Without a terminal, and on CI,
  the "started" lines stay.
- For a failure, instead of the whole stdout and stderr:
  - the exception's traceback;
  - the last lines of stderr;
  - the last 40 lines of test_framework.log;
  - the last 20 warning/error lines of each node's debug.log;
  - the test directory, the command that reruns the test alone, and
    the combine_logs.py command.

  The full output stays in <tmpdir>/<test>.stdout and .stderr.
- After the existing results table (unchanged, as scripts rely on it):
  the 10 slowest tests and every failure with its rerun command.
- A test that fails before running (e.g. on bad arguments) reports the
  error once, instead of a traceback through argparse.

Structured output (documented in README-runner-output.md):
- --jsonl-file=FILE: one JSON object per test start and result, and a
  final summary.
- --json-summary=FILE: counts, wall and accumulated time, and the failed
  tests.
- --junitoutput now also has skip reasons, failure type, message and
  traceback, and per-phase durations as properties.

Unit tests cover the result line, the failure block (log tails, node
warnings/errors), the summary and the JSON lines. The full functional
suite gives the same per-test results as before.
